# dnasrep DNS redirect rules
#
# Copy this file to "dns.config" (next to the binary, or point at it with
# -dns-config) to add hostnames the redirector should answer itself.
#
# One rule per line:
#
#     <name> [ip]
#
#   <name>  a hostname or domain suffix. A suffix matches the name itself and
#           any subdomain, so "dnas.playstation.org" also covers
#           "gate1.us.dnas.playstation.org".
#   [ip]    optional target IPv4 address. If omitted, the global -redirect-ip
#           (this server) is used.
#
# The most specific (longest) matching rule wins, and rules here override the
# built-in -dns-suffix defaults for the same name. Blank lines and lines
# starting with '#' are ignored.

# The DNAS gateways -> this server (uses -redirect-ip):
dnas.playstation.org

# A KDDI game server (e.g. for some JP titles) -> a specific host:
www01.kddi-mmbb.jp        192.168.2.30
